# Trivy ignore file — accepted findings, each with an expiry (exp:YYYY-MM-DD).
# After the expiry Trivy stops honouring the line and the pipeline fails again,
# forcing a re-review. Keep every entry justified.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Framework CVEs blocked by upstream peer ranges — tracked in infra/RUNBOOK.md
# ("Still open"). Re-evaluate by 2026-10-10.
#
# next 15.4.11 (+ the postcss 8.4.31 it vendors): fixes land in next >= 15.5.16,
#   but @payloadcms/next@3.88.0 pins next to ">=15.4.11 <15.5.0 || >=16.2.6".
#   Requires upgrading Payload (3.88 -> a release supporting next 15.5+/16).
# astro 5.18.2: fixes land in astro 6.3.3 / 6.4.6 / 7.2.8 — a two-major
#   migration (5 -> 7). Scheduled as its own work item.
#
# Mitigating context: the image-optimization RCEs (GHSA-26w7-cxv4-gfx2,
# GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4, CVE-2026-75604) require attacker-supplied images hitting
# the optimizer; the frontend serves only build-time /_astro assets and the
# Payload media pipeline is admin-auth gated. Not a substitute for the upgrade.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

